<<~ ahu #/ruling>>

! Recipe Layer Model ~ a scout against the ruling

''Register: Scout-Handoff.'' A tasked spirit read the mount code, the routing cascade, the sync gate, the disk legs, the TW5 fork and the standing canon, whole, and hands back what it found. Every claim below names a file and a line; a claim without one names itself as inference. Nothing here changes code.

''The operator's ruling, verbatim (quote license):''

> "For each recipe, the 'top bag' gets determined by the kind of raw tiddler. Most go to the 'named wiki bag' (disk projects into the base `/wikis/*` dir for the recipe), BUT `Draft of '...'` and similar tiddlers (#has `draft-of` field, etc) goes to a 'drafts' layer above that (fleet synced just as the wiki's main wiki-bag and the underlying canon-bags). Then there's volatile tiddlers on top of that (most don't sync, I think all here don't, Presence, local-only state, THIS is the per-device layer). Under the `wikis/` layers we have the 'canon bags' from `bags/` (disk ingest/projection-on-move). We need to deeply scout this blur and resolve the code and memes to one 'model architecture'. … Now that we have 'api surface' for memes and not just tiddlers this becomes important to clarify for all incoming files (other files would get ingested as typed tiddlers and round trip to disk with `*.meta` files, etc, so we may need to stub out or find the TW5 api surfaces for those non-tiddler/non-meme workflows)."

The ruling names FOUR strata per recipe — ''canon bags'' ← ''named wiki bag'' ← ''drafts'' ← ''volatile'' — and one routing key: ''the kind of raw tiddler''. The code today mounts FIVE per-wiki slots plus a canon and a library floor, and routes by ''title prefix''. The rest of this carrier measures the distance.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-mounted>>

!! The layers exactly as three composites mount them today

Three `CompositeStore` instances stand in a running node, and one shape serves the browser. Bottom row first (lowest priority); the top row wins a read. ''`default`'' marks the layer the composite's UNBAGGED writes fall into — `addLayer` re-points `writableStore` at every layer registered with `writable:true` and `defaultWritable !== false` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts:123`), so the LAST such layer holds the office (`composite-store.ts:304-310`).

''Sync class'' reads off the node `sharePolicy`: every Automerge doc full-syncs to an in-process island peer and to a `same-operator` WS peer (the device fleet); a cross-operator peer reaches only the deterministically-federatable planes (`packages/lararium-node/src/self-slot-share.ts:70-95`, `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:434-462`). So ''fleet'' below means //any Automerge doc//; ''device'' means //a `MemoryTiddlerStore` that never enters a Repo//. The browser gate carries the same split (`packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts:370`, `:523`).

!!! A. The wiki ISLAND composite (node and browser — one kernel)

Laid by `expandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts:265-286`) walked bottom-up in `buildIslandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-recipe.ts:66-82`); slot docs resolve from typed grants in `sovereign-kernel.ts:306-334`.

| layer (top wins) | store | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by | disk mirror (node) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | `MemoryTiddlerStore` | yes | ''YES'' (`island-recipe.ts:70`) | device | none — fresh per boot | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no (`:80`) | fleet | `daemon/draft-bindings/{fingerprint}`, PersonaGroup × recipe-fingerprint (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts:661-664`; `resolve-binding.ts:108-125`) | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/personal` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | `daemon/personal-bindings/{fingerprint}` (same) | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/working` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | `daemon/working-bindings/{fingerprint}` (same) | `wikis/{slug}/` via the `wikiSlot:"working"` grant (`open-node-vessel.ts:1650`, `vessel-island-pool-core.ts:84-107`) |
| `bags/{slug}` (canon) | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | `grants.wikiUrl` = the catalog's `bags/{slug}` oracle | `bags/{slug}/` via the `selfCanon` grant (`:1655`) |
| `libraryBags[]` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | catalog registry, reconciled live (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/recipe-watch.ts:130-148`) | `bags/lares/`, `bags/lararium/`, `bags/crossroads/` for the literal grants (`:1632-1639`) |
| `bags/oracle` (floor) | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | `grants.islandUrl` | none |

Two facts the table hides. (1) ''Every CRDT slot registers `writable:true`'' — the island refuses nothing at the store; the cascade alone decides where a save lands (`island-recipe.ts:76-80`). (2) ''The composite's default writable reads `wikis/{slug}/temp`'' — the volatile store, registered last. Consequence measured by reading, not by running: an in-wiki DELETE calls `store.tombstone(title, origin)` with no bag (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts:293`) → `composite.tombstone` → `this.writableStore` (`composite-store.ts:250-253`) → the temp store. The kāpae hides the lower record for this session and the record ''returns at the next boot''. The routing-totality test asserts only that `tombstone` fires, never which bag (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/routing-totality.test.ts:203-209`). ''A red test owes this before any fix.''

!!! B. The daemon ISLAND composite (`recipe: { wikiSlug: "daemon" }`)

Same kernel (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-daemon-vm.ts:94`; browser `open-browser-vessel.ts:807`). The grants carry `islandUrl`, `wikiUrl` (= the daemon bag) and `catalogUrl` only (`open-node-vessel.ts:1065-1071`), so `slotUrl` returns null for draft/working/personal and those slots ''prune for want of a handle'' (`sovereign-kernel.ts:327-334`); `crossroads` splices in as a library (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts:553-554`).

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | disk mirror |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/daemon/temp` | yes | ''YES'' | device | none |
| `bags/daemon` (the daemon bag, as its own "canon") | yes | no | fleet (private plane) | none — excluded by design |
| `bags/crossroads` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | `bags/crossroads/` on the wiki-island grant, none here |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` | yes | no | fleet | none here |
| `bags/oracle` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | none |

`current-wiki-bag` seeds to the daemon bag itself because no `working` handle exists (`island-recipe.ts:97`). A `Draft of ` title in the daemon wiki routes to `wikis/daemon/draft` (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/lar-bag-paths.tid:16`) — a bag with NO layer — and `composite.put` refuses loud (`composite-store.ts:236-244`). Read from the code; unmeasured live.

!!! C. The HOST composite (VM-free, one per vessel)

`assembleVessel` + `mountWikiSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/open-vessel-core.ts:159-291`, `:294-327`), invoked by `wikiCap` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:155`).

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | yes | ''YES'' (`:324`) | device | fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | yes | no (`:322`) | fleet | catalog `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{vessel-DID}` (`:317-321`; `wiki-recipe.ts:96-99`) |
| `bags/{slug}` | yes | ''yes'' (`:315`) | fleet | catalog `bags/{slug}` |
| PersonaGroup · circles · identities · sessions · `bags/daemon` | yes | ''yes'' (`:258`, no `defaultWritable` given → true) | fleet (private) | bootstrap |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` | yes | no (`:150`) | fleet | oracle well-known tiddlers |
| `bags/oracle` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | genesis |
| `bags/catalog` | ''no'' (`:154`) | — | fleet (private) | catalog-url file |

Three layers here carry `defaultWritable: true`; the temp store wins by registering last. The host mounts NO `working` and NO `personal` layer, and its draft doc keys per ''vessel DID'', not per PersonaGroup × fingerprint — the same slot name `wikis/{slug}/draft` names ''two different documents'' on the host and in the island (the #/the-blur names this).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-routed>>

!! The cascade ~ which KIND of tiddler lands where today

The in-wiki cascade `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/bag-paths` (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/lar-bag-paths.tid:5-18`) walks newline-separated filters against the saving title; first non-empty result names the slot, an empty operand from a NAMED rule withholds, and no match names a router gap that still lands at `current-wiki-bag` with a console warning (`island-adaptor.ts:118-160`). Every rule reads the ''title''; no rule reads a field (`island-adaptor.ts:284-289` states why: a delete runs after the tiddler has gone).

| kind of raw tiddler | rule (`lar-bag-paths.tid`) | lands in | sync |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$:/core`, `$:/library/sjcl.js` | `:5-6` withhold | nowhere (engine bytes ride CAS) | — |
| `$:/temp/*`, `$:/status/*`, `$:/boot/*`, `$:/HistoryList*` | `:7-10` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| `$:/StoryList*`, `$:/state/folded/*`, `$:/state/tab-*`, `$:/palette*` | `:11-14` | `wikis/{slug}/personal` | fleet |
| every other `$:/state/*` | `:15` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| `Draft of *` (title prefix, English default only) | `:16` | `wikis/{slug}/draft` | fleet |
| `lar:*` | `:17` | `current-wiki-bag` = `wikis/{slug}/working` (daemon: `bags/daemon`) | fleet |
| anything else, including a foreign-titled pack member (`HelloThere`) and every other `$:/` system tiddler | `:18` catch-all | `current-wiki-bag` | fleet |

''`draft-of` reads nowhere.'' TW5 itself decides draft-ness by the `draft.of` FIELD (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/tiddler.js:20-22`), and it mints the title through a LOCALIZED language string — `Draft/Title`, or `Draft/Attribution` when `$:/status/UserName` stands, yielding `Draft of 'X' by <user>` (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/wiki.js:1725-1735`). The prefix rule holds for the English default with no user name and breaks for a ja-JP edition or a named user. The ruling's spelling `draft-of` (hyphen) names no TW5 field; TW5 spells it `draft.of`.

''What the nalu stamps.'' Every inbound record gains `$origin-bag` from the ENVELOPE (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/nalu-engine.ts:112-116`); the projector routes a flush by that stamp (`packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:280-283`), and the outbound save strips it before the put (`island-adaptor.ts:352-355`). No persisted field names a bag.

!!! Verb seats

| seat | resolves the bag how | lands in | file:line |
|---|---|---|---|
| in-wiki edit / save | the cascade, by title | per the table above | `island-adaptor.ts:340-371` |
| in-wiki delete | NO bag — `composite.tombstone` | the default writable = ''temp'' | `island-adaptor.ts:284-296`, `composite-store.ts:250` |
| `meme put` (no target) | the daemon's own `$tw.wiki` → its cascade → `current-wiki-bag` | `bags/daemon` | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts:170-173`, `:189-190` |
| `meme put --recipe <slug>` | the recipe RECORD's `writable-bag`, else the top of its `bag-stack` (`designatedBagOf`, `:121-129`) → a mounted writable layer of the DAEMON island, else reach by catalog under `wikis/<slug>/drafts/<DID>` | the per-DID draft doc the HOST mounts — a doc the wiki island never lays | `meme-verbs.ts:131-153` |
| `meme get --recipe <slug>` | same designated bag, `storeForBag` else reach | reads ONE bag, never the stack | `meme-verbs.ts:136-137`, `:185-188` |
| `meme put --bag <slug>` | `compositeMemeSink` → `composite.put({bag})` on the daemon island | that bag's writable layer, else refuses (no shadow-up) | `meme-verbs.ts:177-179`, `composite-store.ts:218-244` |
| `act ADD / COPY / MOVE / LOAD / INGEST --to <bag>` | `BagAccess`: a mounted writable layer, else the catalog/oracle accessor's own store (write-then-sync) | the named bag exactly | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts:243-270`, `:1170-1186` |
| `lares ingest --source <dir> --to <bag>` | the caller names `--to`; a `wikis/` source only changes the URI derivation | the named bag | `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/ingest.ts:27-33`, `packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:118-131` |
| `draft` verb (`makeDraftReactor`) | `toBag` else `defaultWritableBagId()` | ''temp'' by default | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-draft-handlers.ts:14-19` |
| recipe-watch library mount | `bag-stack` minus the structural set | inserted above `bags/lares`, `writable:true, defaultWritable:false` | `recipe-watch.ts:81-89`, `:105-115` |

`CompositeStore.getRecipe` / `putViaRecipe` (`composite-store.ts:544-562`, `:597-611`) read `fields["bagStack"]` / `writableBag` in camelCase; every writer spells `bag-stack` / `writable-bag` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/genesis-doc.ts:372-388`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-mint-handlers.ts:84-85`). No production caller reaches either method (only `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/composite-store.test.ts`). Dead surface, reading a field nothing writes.

