<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-blur>>

!! The blur, named

# ''`writable-bag` (draft) vs the mount's default (canon on the host, temp in the island).'' The recipe record designates `wikis/{slug}/draft`; the host composite's LAST default-writable layer reads temp (`open-vessel-core.ts:324`), the canon bag holds the flag beneath it (`:315`), and the island's reads temp too (`island-recipe.ts:70`). `meme put --recipe` obeys the record; an in-wiki save obeys the cascade (`working`); a bagless put obeys the composite (temp). Three writers, three answers to "the top bag".
# ''Two draft documents wear one slot name.'' The island's `wikis/{slug}/draft` binds per (PersonaGroup × fingerprint) through the daemon doc (`resolve-binding.ts:108-125`), delegated to the PersonaGroup, so it ''fleet-syncs today'' — a `Draft of` typed on one device reaches the operator's other devices, as the ruling wants. The host's `wikis/{slug}/draft` binds per vessel DID in the catalog (`wikiDraftDocKey`, `wiki-recipe.ts:96-99`), and `meme put --recipe` lands there (`meme-verbs.ts:144-147`). The wiki island never mounts the per-DID doc; a meme placed by `--recipe` never surfaces in the running wiki until something else moves it. `prune-stale` reads the per-DID doc (`wiki-draft-handlers.ts:70-76`).
# ''Per-DID or per-PersonaGroup — the code holds both, the canon says one.'' `personal-slot#/scoping-mechanism` rules (PersonaGroup × fingerprint); `wiki init` mints per DID. Which one the ruling means by "fleet synced" decides which doc survives.
# ''What "volatile / per-device" holds today: temp ALONE.'' Presence stands unbuilt — no `presence` slot, no `$:/status/` beyond what TW5 writes; `$:/status/*` and `$:/boot/*` and most `$:/state/*` route to temp (`lar-bag-paths.tid:8-10`, `:15`). `personal` fleet-syncs by design (view state), so the ruling's "all here don't [sync]" holds for temp and not for personal. Per-device state that MUST survive a reboot (a device's own window layout, a local-only bag pin) has no home: temp forgets at boot, personal follows the fleet.
# ''`Draft of` routes by TITLE PREFIX alone.'' Field-based routing cannot ride the cascade as built: a delete runs after the tiddler has gone, so any rule reading `draft.of` would route the creation and drop the deletion (`island-adaptor.ts:284-289`). The ruling's "#has `draft-of` field" therefore asks for a second read path — the field on SAVE, the last-known slot on DELETE — or for the title rule to stay and the field to stay advisory.
# ''A non-meme file enters by three doors and leaves by one, and foreign titles leave by none.'' Enter: (a) `lares ingest --source --to` scans `.mem` and any extension, pairs a `.meta` sidecar, derives the URI by the loci law (`ingest-core.ts:83-88`, `:111-113`, `:171-181`); the island runs `tw5.parseFields(meta)` then `tw5.deserialize(ext, text, base)` (`action-handler.ts:863-873`) and packs foreign-titled members into `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`:815-833`). (b) `act LOAD --to` takes carriers with the verb, same registry route (`:641-707`). (c) the in-wiki drag-drop / `$:/Import` ride TW5's own DOM deserializer and then the cascade — no house code touches it. Leave: the ONE render shore `exportCarrierFile` (`meme-write.ts:40-77`) → `makeTw5FileInfo` (`tw5-file-info.ts:88-176`) picks `.tid` / content + `.meta` / `.json` exactly as `generateTiddlerFileInfo` does, base64 for a binary type (`:140`), and the projector sites it at `<uri-path><ext>` (`disk-projector.ts:352-360`). But `carrierBaseRelPath` sites only `lar:///w.w.w/…` names (`bag-paths.ts:84-99`): a `.png` ingested under a loci URI round-trips; a `HelloThere.tid` pack member reaches disk only through REPACK of its pack (`action-handler.ts:352-370`).
# ''`meme get --recipe` reads the designated bag, not the stack'' (`meme-verbs.ts:136-137`, `:185`). A meme living in canon under a recipe whose `writable-bag` names draft reads as absent. The in-wiki face reads the stack. The two verbs disagree by construction.
# ''Two recipe shapes, one name.'' The recipe RECORD (`bag-stack` + `writable-bag`) drives `meme put --recipe`, recipe-watch's library membership, and nothing else. The `WikiRecipe` struct (`{ wikiSlug, libraryBags?, mirrorBags? }`) drives the mount. `catalog` sits in the user `bag-stack` (`wiki-mint-handlers.ts:84`) and recipe-watch treats it as a library to mount (`recipe-watch.ts:134-146`; `urlOfBag(catalog)` resolves null, so it skips — by accident, not by law).
# ''`working` and `personal` stand outside the ruling's four strata.'' The ruling names canon ← named wiki bag ← drafts ← volatile. The code lays canon ← ''working'' ← ''personal'' ← draft ← temp. Either "named wiki bag" means `working` (the saved live layer, projecting to `wikis/{slug}/`) and canon means `bags/{slug}` — which matches the ruling's disk sentence exactly — or the ruling collapses working into the canon bag and the shore-law promotion MOVE goes. The disk sentence decides it: "disk projects into the base `/wikis/*` dir" names `working`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/one-model>>

!! One model ~ the fewest changes that satisfy the ruling

''The layer list per recipe'' (bottom → top), reading the ruling's four strata onto the slots that already exist:

| ruling stratum | slot | store | sync | disk | writable | default |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| canon bags | `bags/oracle` · `libraryBags[]` · `bags/{slug}` | CRDT | fleet (+ federatable where the plane allows) | `bags/{name}/` on ingest and on promotion MOVE | by ACTION verb only | no |
| named wiki bag | `wikis/{slug}/working` | CRDT | fleet | `wikis/{slug}/` | the cascade's catch-all | ''YES — the ONE default'' |
| drafts | `wikis/{slug}/draft` (absorbs `personal` as a KIND, see below) | CRDT | fleet | none | the cascade's draft rule | no |
| volatile | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | memory | device | none | the cascade's temp rules | no |

''Changes this asks of code:''

* ''The default writable moves to `working`'' — `island-recipe.ts:70` sets temp `defaultWritable:false`; `:80` sets the working slot `defaultWritable:true` when its handle stands (else the canon bag, the daemon's case); `open-vessel-core.ts:315-324` mirrors it (working absent on the host today → the canon bag keeps the flag; temp drops it). This alone cures the delete-to-temp resurrection and gives the `draft` verb a durable fallback.
* ''The delete routes like the save'' — `island-adaptor.ts:293` becomes `tombstoneInBag(destination, title)` through the cascade verdict it already computed at `:289`. Red test first in `routing-totality.test.ts`.
* ''One draft document.'' Retire the per-DID `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{DID}` key: `wiki init` stops minting it (`wiki-mint-handlers.ts:36`, `:48-66`), `mountWikiSlot` stops resolving it (`open-vessel-core.ts:317-322`), `meme-verbs.ts:144-147` and `wiki-draft-handlers.ts:70-76` read the PersonaGroup × fingerprint binding through the daemon composite instead (`DRAFT_BINDINGS_PREFIX`, `lar-uris.ts:539`). `wiki-recipe.ts:96-99` (`wikiDraftDocKey`) goes. A weld test on the four sites before the rename.
* ''The routing KEY reads the kind of raw tiddler, in this order'', all on the title so the delete path survives: `$:/temp/*` · `$:/status/*` · `$:/boot/*` · `$:/HistoryList*` → volatile; the TW5 draft title (the `Draft/Title` AND `Draft/Attribution` shapes — read the language strings at boot into a `current-wiki-draft-prefix` config tiddler rather than hardcoding English; `island-recipe.ts:95-104` already seeds config) → drafts; `$:/StoryList*` · `$:/state/*` · `$:/palette*` → drafts-as-view-state (see the fork below); everything else → working. The `draft.of` FIELD stays advisory: a save whose fields carry `draft.of` and whose title misses the prefix logs a router warning (`island-adaptor.ts:148-160` already owns the voice), never a second route.
* ''`meme get --recipe` reads the STACK; `meme put --recipe` writes the record's `writable-bag`.'' `reachRecipeBag(…, "get")` (`meme-verbs.ts:131-153`) resolves the whole `bag-stack` top-down through `storeForBag`/reach and returns the first live record; put keeps the designated bag. Two verbs, two laws, stated in `meme-verbs.ts:1-30`.
* ''The recipe record and the mount struct converge on one spelling.'' `expandRecipe` reads `libraryBags` off the record's `bag-stack` (minus the structural set recipe-watch already names, `recipe-watch.ts:87-89`) at mount (`vessel-steps.ts:148-151`), and `writable-bag` names `wikis/{slug}/working` in both minters (`genesis-doc.ts:379-388`, `wiki-mint-handlers.ts:84-85`); `catalog` leaves the user `bag-stack`. `getRecipe`/`putViaRecipe` (`composite-store.ts:544-611`) retire or read the hyphenated fields.
* ''Disk legs for non-meme files:'' wire `pathFilters`/`extFilters` from `config/disk-paths` · `config/disk-extensions` into `exportCarrierFile` (`meme-write.ts:57`, `:76`) so rule 3 of `disk-projection#/projection-routing` stands; a foreign-titled record keeps its pack (REPACK) — the ruling's "round trip to disk with `*.meta` files" already holds for loci-titled content files (`tw5-file-info.ts:118-121`, `:162-165`; `disk-projector.ts:352-360`). No new TW5 surface needed; the house already rides `deserializeTiddlers`, `parseFields`, `contentTypeInfo`, `getFileExtensionInfo` and a pure re-implementation of `generateTiddlerFileInfo`.

''Verb-seat mapping under the model:'' in-wiki save/delete → cascade by kind; `meme put` (anchor) → the daemon's working layer once the late-attach lands (`wiki-layer-ontology#/the-daemon-wiki`), its own bag until then; `meme put --recipe` → that wiki's `working`; `meme put --bag` · `act ADD/COPY/MOVE/LOAD/INGEST --to` · `lares ingest --to` → the named bag exactly, canon included, effect-record audited; promotion `working → bags/{slug}` stays a MOVE.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/questions>>

!! Questions only the operator answers

# ''Does a `Draft of` tiddler fleet-sync, or stay on the device that drafted it?'' The ruling says fleet; the island already does fleet; the host's per-DID doc says device. Fork: keep the PersonaGroup × fingerprint binding (retire `wikiDraftDocKey`) — or keep per-DID and re-key the island's binding to the DID.
# ''Does `personal` survive as a layer, or fold into `drafts` as a KIND of draft (view state)?'' The ruling names four strata and `personal` sits in none. Fork: five slots with `personal` between draft and working as today — or four slots, `$:/StoryList` · `$:/state/*` routed to `draft` with a `kind` marker, one binding fewer per fingerprint.
# ''Which per-device state MUST survive a reboot?'' Temp forgets; personal follows the fleet. If a device's own layout or a local pin needs to persist, the volatile stratum splits into `temp` (memory) and a per-device CRDT doc that never enters the fleet share set — a fourth sync class the gate does not carry today (`self-slot-share.ts:70-95` knows same-operator, cross-operator, in-process).
# ''Does "named wiki bag" mean `working` (saved live, `wikis/{slug}/`) with canon reached by promotion MOVE — or does the wiki write straight into `bags/{slug}`?'' The ruling's disk sentence says `working`; `wiki-layer-ontology#/quine` rules the same; the recipe records say draft. Fork: keep the shore-law MOVE — or retire `working` and let the canon bag take saves (which puts every edit on the tracked `bags/` tree).
# ''Does `meme get --recipe` read the stack or the top bag?'' The scout proposes the stack; the current code reads the designated bag.
# ''Does the `draft.of` FIELD ever decide routing, or only the title?'' A field-read costs a last-known-slot map for deletes.
# ''Which non-meme file types enter through `lares ingest` today, versus drag-drop only?'' `ingest` scans every extension and hands them to TW5's registry (`ingest-core.ts:111-113`, `action-handler.ts:872`); the operator decides whether a `.png` under `bags/` counts as canon (it lands, base64, and projects back as bytes) or whether binaries ride the CAS shelf only (`action-handler.ts:653-659`, the skinny handle).
# ''Does the daemon wiki gain its `working` layer now?'' The late-attach stands designed (`wiki-layer-ontology#/the-daemon-wiki`); until it lands `meme put` without a target writes the daemon bag and a `Draft of` in the daemon wiki refuses loud.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/tw5-surfaces>>

!! TW5 surfaces for non-meme workflows ~ what exists, what the house rides

| surface | where (fork) | does | the house |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$tw.utils.registerFileType` · `$tw.config.contentTypeInfo` · `fileExtensionInfo` · `getFileExtensionInfo` · `getTypeEncoding` | `TiddlyWiki5/boot/boot.js:553-583` | the ONE registry: content-type ↔ extension ↔ encoding ↔ `deserializerType` | rides (`tw5-file-info.ts:135-140`, `action-handler.ts:110-135`) |
| `$tw.wiki.deserializeTiddlers(type, text, srcFields)` | `boot.js:1641-1670` | routes by deserializer name, content type, extension, `deserializerType`, then `text/plain` | rides (`action-handler.ts:127-128`) |
| boot deserializers `tid` · `tids` (multids) · `txt` · `html` · `json` · `js` · `css` · `dom` | `boot.js:1687-1835`; `core/modules/deserializers.js` | the packs (`.json` array, `.multids`, `.html` store-area) | rides through the registry; pack membership aside in `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`action-handler.ts:815-833`) |
| `$tw.utils.parseFields` | `boot.js:428` | `.meta` and `.tid` header parsing | rides (`action-handler.ts:129-132`) |
| `$tw.loadTiddlersFromFile` · `$tw.loadMetadataForFile` · `$tw.loadTiddlersFromPath` · `$tw.loadTiddlersFromSpecification` (`tiddlywiki.files`) · `$tw.loadPluginFolder` · `$tw.loadWikiTiddlers` | `boot.js:1941-1964`, `:1969-1976`, `:1988-2013`, `:2017`, `:2168`, `:2293` | node-only disk walkers; `.meta` sidecar merged onto the first tiddler; `maxEditFileSize` guard; `excludeRegExp` skips `*.meta` (`:1983`) | ''does not ride'' — the house walks disk in `ingest-core.ts` (`git ls-files`-shaped, declaration-read) and hands bytes to the registry; `tiddlywiki.files` specifications and `plugin.info` folders stay unread |
| `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` | `boot.js:2369` | the file-path ↔ title map the folder loader keeps | rides the same title for pack provenance (`action-handler.ts:833`) |
| `generateTiddlerFileInfo` · `generateTiddlerFilepath` · `saveTiddlerToFile(Sync)` · `deleteTiddlerFile` · `cleanupTiddlerFiles` | `TiddlyWiki5/core-server/filesystem.js:213`, `:322`, `:445`, `:487`, `:508`, `:549` | type selection (.tid / content+.meta / .json), path sanitizing, the write | ''re-implemented pure'' in `tw5-file-info.ts:88-176` (no `fs`); the projector writes (`disk-projector.ts:352-400`) |
| `$:/config/FileSystemPaths` · `$:/config/FileSystemExtensions` | `plugins/tiddlywiki/filesystem/filesystemadaptor.js:59-65` | the siting and extension cascades | mirrored as `config/disk-paths` · `config/disk-extensions` in canon; ''unwired'' (`meme-write.ts:57`, `:76` pass no filters) |
| the `filesystem` syncadaptor · `syncer.js` · `$:/config/SyncFilter` | `filesystemadaptor.js:86`; `core/modules/syncer.js:19`, `:67`; `core/wiki/config/SyncFilter.tid` | TW5's own save-to-disk loop and its total-minus-exclusions filter | ''does not ride'' the adaptor; the cascade takes SyncFilter's SHAPE (`island-adaptor.ts:107-111`) |
| `isSystemTiddler` · `isTemporaryTiddler` · `isVolatileTiddler` · `Tiddler.isDraft` · `generateDraftTitle` | `core/modules/wiki.js:222-232`, `:1725`; `core/modules/tiddler.js:20-22` | the kind predicates TW5 itself uses (`$:/` · `$:/temp/` · `$:/temp/volatile/` · the `draft.of` field · the localized draft title) | rides none directly; the cascade re-spells three of them as prefix rules (`lar-bag-paths.tid:7`, `:15`, `:16`) |
| `--load` · `--save` · `--savetiddlers` · `--savewikifolder` · `--render` · `--import` · `--unpackplugin` | `TiddlyWiki5/core-server/commands/` | the CLI legs for a folder wiki | `--render`'s law rides in `meme-project.ts:104`; the rest stay stubs the house never calls |
| `$:/Import` · dropzone · `th-importing-tiddler` | `core/modules/widgets/` (dropzone, navigator) | in-browser file drop → DOM deserializer → the wiki | rides untouched; a dropped file then saves through the cascade like any edit |
| MWS (multi-wiki server) | absent from this fork (`plugins/tiddlywiki/` holds `filesystem` and `tiddlyweb` only) | — | nothing to ride |

''Reading.'' The house already stands on the registry and the deserializer chain, and re-implements the filesystem module's pure half. What it lacks names itself: the siting cascades (designed, unwired), the disk walker's `tiddlywiki.files` and plugin-folder legs (never needed while `ingest` reads declarations), and a kind predicate that reads TW5's own `draft.of` and language strings instead of an English prefix.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>

!! Aftermath ~ the blast-radius spiral (operator-approved)

The spiral walked every carrier the #/as-written table names and evergreened the ones whose text described retired code: `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (drafts → `@draft`, volatile → `@temp`, title-read), `save-path` SP-3/SP-4 (the cascade rule; the envelope law, no `bag` field routes), `disk-projection#/projection-routing` (the siting requirement for rule 2; rule 3 marked OWED), `residency-model#/tai-chi` (temp outside the keyed set), `bag-wiki-uri-split` meta (`standing`, half-enactment named). The `lares-history` tree stays untouched (history, never canon).

''Tensions the spiral did NOT resolve — surfaced, not rewritten'' (a law vs the code, and only the operator rules which one yields):

# `wiki-layer-ontology#/naming-law` — "instance mounts MUST NOT enter `@catalog`" — against the per-DID draft key `wiki init` registers there. The law stands; the code violates it; #/one-model proposes retiring the key.
# `personal-slot#/scoping-mechanism` — draft per (PersonaGroup × fingerprint) — against the host's per-DID draft doc. Same fork as above, read from the other carrier.
# The ruling's FOUR strata against the code's FIVE slots (`working` + `personal` unnamed by the ruling) — #/questions 2 and 4.
# The ruling's `draft-of` FIELD against the cascade's title-only law — #/questions 6.
# The composite default writable = temp (the delete-to-temp resurrection) — a code defect read, not measured; owed a red test before any fix.

